#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35727
#: 22bb6e0d4b84458cbf8f4e50fb773e98
msgid "EK3\\_DRAG\\_BCOEF\\_X: Ballistic coefficient for X axis drag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35731
#: 677b016282384a0aa28173dfb81fab57
msgid "Ratio of mass to drag coefficient measured along the X body axis\\. This parameter enables estimation of wind drift for vehicles with bluff bodies and without propulsion forces in the X and Y direction \\(eg multicopters\\)\\. The drag produced by this effect scales with speed squared\\. Set to a positive value \\> 1\\.0 to enable\\. A starting value is the mass in Kg divided by the frontal area\\. The predicted drag from the rotors is specified separately by the EK3\\_DRAG\\_MCOEF parameter\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35737
#: 1cca7a499e274594a16d04d76eaf8215
msgid "0.0 to 1000.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35737
#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35756
#: bffdffa399e044acaf8ce9abad67bb2b
#: ec15bca1b22445b296beccffb1478305
msgid "kilograms per square meter"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35746
#: e3b3a9b39e384233b6741da68779c718
msgid "EK3\\_DRAG\\_BCOEF\\_Y: Ballistic coefficient for Y axis drag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35750
#: 5f056f9c96114955bdfc66f72d435a63
msgid "Ratio of mass to drag coefficient measured along the Y body axis\\. This parameter enables estimation of wind drift for vehicles with bluff bodies and without propulsion forces in the X and Y direction \\(eg multicopters\\)\\. The drag produced by this effect scales with speed squared\\. Set to a positive value \\> 1\\.0 to enable\\. A starting value is the mass in Kg divided by the side area\\. The predicted drag from the rotors is specified separately by the EK3\\_DRAG\\_MCOEF parameter\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35756
#: 41e788deaf3245ce8ee1c83d54ad99fd
msgid "50.0 to 1000.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35765
#: 5899069195574aeea2d8f8a840772ceb
msgid "EK3\\_DRAG\\_M\\_NSE: Observation noise for drag acceleration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35769
#: 7dfdddd5ded1497da721598f6715eb10
msgid "This sets the amount of noise used when fusing X and Y acceleration as an observation that enables estimation of wind velocity for multi\\-rotor vehicles\\. This feature is enabled by the EK3\\_DRAG\\_BCOEF\\_X and EK3\\_DRAG\\_BCOEF\\_Y parameters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35775
#: ab88963b47ab43b094870ca53dbced7d
msgid "0.1 to 2.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35784
#: 0f315513659044798894c0afb50f87da
msgid "EK3\\_DRAG\\_MCOEF: Momentum coefficient for propeller drag"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35788
#: 01fec820e92b4c21b9f8ea4d51afc42e
msgid "This parameter is used to predict the drag produced by the rotors when flying a multi\\-copter\\, enabling estimation of wind drift\\. The drag produced by this effect scales with speed not speed squared and is produced because some of the air velocity normal to the rotors axis of rotation is lost when passing through the rotor disc which changes the momentum of the airflow causing drag\\. For unducted rotors the effect is roughly proportional to the area of the propeller blades when viewed side on and changes with different propellers\\. It is higher for ducted rotors\\. For example if flying at 15 m\\/s at sea level conditions produces a rotor induced drag acceleration of 1\\.5 m\\/s\\/s\\, then EK3\\_DRAG\\_MCOEF would be set to 0\\.1 \\= \\(1\\.5\\/15\\.0\\)\\. Set EK3\\_MCOEF to a positive value to enable wind estimation using this drag effect\\. To account for the drag produced by the body which scales with speed squared\\, see documentation for the EK3\\_DRAG\\_BCOEF\\_X and EK3\\_DRAG\\_BCOEF\\_Y parameters\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35794
#: fd6fcf64fe8d4094b7857154b36591bd
msgid "per second"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35803
#: cc359ab20af149b9876170286e34cfe3
msgid "EK3\\_OGNM\\_TEST\\_SF: On ground not moving test scale factor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35807
#: c0d992f9de5f4cc1ac358a0c550278ce
msgid "This parameter is adjust the sensitivity of the on ground not moving test which is used to assist with learning the yaw gyro bias and stopping yaw drift before flight when operating without a yaw sensor\\. Bigger values allow the detection of a not moving condition with noiser IMU data\\. Check the XKFM data logged when the vehicle is on ground not moving and adjust the value of OGNM\\_TEST\\_SF to be slightly higher than the maximum value of the XKFM\\.ADR\\, XKFM\\.ALR\\, XKFM\\.GDR and XKFM\\.GLR test levels\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35813
#: 781756d73f83416e8a944392c1c2cb29
msgid "1.0 to 10.0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35822
#: 1ec57e1d7b994cf7bf604f1face69128
msgid "EK3\\_GND\\_EFF\\_DZ: Baro height ground effect dead zone"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35826
#: e9d0fc5dce214d04aa1bddbc660bf98b
msgid "This parameter sets the size of the dead zone that is applied to negative baro height spikes that can occur when taking off or landing when a vehicle with lift rotors is operating in ground effect ground effect\\. Set to about 0\\.5m less than the amount of negative offset in baro height that occurs just prior to takeoff when lift motors are spooling up\\. Set to 0 if no ground effect is present\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35841
#: 7a7d474c4f41401283938f1e17cb9427
msgid "EK3\\_PRIMARY: Primary core number"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35845
#: 093537b5e96548c2ab7f4b54e41b06cb
msgid "The core number \\(index in IMU mask\\) that will be used as the primary EKF core on startup\\. While disarmed the EKF will force the use of this core\\. A value of 0 corresponds to the first IMU in EK3\\_IMU\\_MASK\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35860
#: ce832b1872bc4630acbf30b5ae780717
msgid "EK3\\_LOG\\_LEVEL: Logging Level"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35864
#: 8e802e865eae45b4abb1324406917b53
msgid "Determines how verbose the EKF3 streaming logging is\\. A value of 0 provides full logging\\(default\\)\\, a value of 1 only XKF4 scaled innovations are logged\\, a value of 2 both XKF4 and GSF are logged\\, and a value of 3 disables all streaming logging of EKF3\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35879
#: 4b98e70e191f4886ab84b313b18c1272
msgid "EK3\\_GPS\\_VACC\\_MAX: GPS vertical accuracy threshold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35883
#: e94138e90a964ddc895fc3082d2f194b
msgid "Vertical accuracy threshold for GPS as the altitude source\\. The GPS will not be used as an altitude source if the reported vertical accuracy of the GPS is larger than this threshold\\, falling back to baro instead\\. Set to zero to deactivate the threshold check\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35898
#: f2a7947e768a40db911546ba4143f569
msgid "EK3\\_OPTIONS: Optional EKF behaviour"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35902
#: 4b6c15d0433940cba70776df10f35153
msgid "EKF optional behaviour\\. Bit 0 \\(JammingExpected\\)\\: Setting JammingExpected will change the EKF behaviour such that if dead reckoning navigation is possible it will require the preflight alignment GPS quality checks controlled by EK3\\_GPS\\_CHECK and EK3\\_CHECK\\_SCALE to pass before resuming GPS use if GPS lock is lost for more than 2 seconds to prevent bad position estimate\\. Bit 1 \\(Manual lane switching\\)\\: DANGEROUS \\– If enabled\\, this disables automatic lane switching\\. If the active lane becomes unhealthy\\, no automatic switching will occur\\. Users must manually set EK3\\_PRIMARY to change lanes\\. No health checks will be performed on the selected lane\\. Use with extreme caution\\.  Bit 2 \\(Optflow may use terrain alt\\)\\: Terrain SRTM data will be used if the vehicle climbs above the rangefinder\\'s range allowing optical flow to be used at higher altitudes\\."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35911
#: 295ccb22bc0c4205846b94e5503ba541
msgid "JammingExpected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35913
#: 8ca408cf2c314afb9562cb85d36c21b5
msgid "ManualLaneSwitching"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/parameters.rst:35915
#: 0b5cf1b7b5f04a389afc085df456749b
msgid "Optflow may use terrain alt"
msgstr ""

